      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In my experience, this comes from video playback within worlds.  VRchat uses a (at time of writing) presently OUTDATED version of the AVPro plugin for Unity to decode video.  The version they are using doesn't like AMD GPUs and it causes a bunch of strange behaviors.  One of those is GPU Timeouts (YES on version 22.11.2, which is the latest as of writing).  It also causes video playback to stutter or artifact.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
